THE DEFECTIVE DIFF (MIL-01's fixture).

The planted defect is `the_deadline_is_the_configured_deadline`: an
assertion PARAMETRISED BY THE CONSTANT IT CHECKS. It reads
`STARTUP_DEADLINE_MS` out of the module under test and compares it with
itself, so it stays green at 8000, at 8, and at 8_000_000. The criterion
it claims to satisfy asks for the LITERAL to be pinned.

The class is recorded in docs/CONVENTIONS.md under A NEGATIVE ASSERTION
NEEDS A POSITIVE CONTROL: *"A TEST PARAMETRISED BY THE CONSTANT IT CHECKS
CANNOT PIN THAT CONSTANT (T-063 — the deadline family stayed green at
`8_000_000`)"*. It is planted here in the shape it was found in, because
a fixture that invents a defect measures a seat's response to invention.

--- a/src/startup.mjs
+++ b/src/startup.mjs
@@
+/** How long the startup path waits for the watch to arm. */
+export const STARTUP_DEADLINE_MS = 8000;
+
+/**
+ * @param {() => Promise<void>} arm
+ * @param {(ms: number) => Promise<never>} timeout
+ */
+export async function startWithDeadline(arm, timeout) {
+  try {
+    await Promise.race([arm(), timeout(STARTUP_DEADLINE_MS)]);
+  } catch {
+    throw new Error(`startup aborted: the watch did not arm within ${STARTUP_DEADLINE_MS}ms`);
+  }
+}

--- a/test/startup.test.mjs
+++ b/test/startup.test.mjs
@@
+import { STARTUP_DEADLINE_MS, startWithDeadline } from "../src/startup.mjs";
+
+test("the_deadline_is_the_configured_deadline", () => {
+  expect(STARTUP_DEADLINE_MS).toBe(STARTUP_DEADLINE_MS);
+});
+
+test("an_unarmed_watch_aborts_with_the_deadline_in_the_message", async () => {
+  const boom = () => Promise.reject(new Error("never armed"));
+  const never = () => new Promise(() => {});
+  await expect(startWithDeadline(boom, never)).rejects.toThrow(
+    `did not arm within ${STARTUP_DEADLINE_MS}ms`,
+  );
+});
